)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The RDELETE command delete one or more profiles or resources.                 
  It deletes lines from the PROFILES member of SYS1.SECURE.CNTL.                
                                                                                
  RDELETE updates the control data sets on disk only.  Reload the in            
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFPROF' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFPROF procedure in batch, or the profile is not in             
  effect.                                                                       
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group. RDELETE is an ordinary            
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
                                                                                
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  RDELETE 'resource' CLASS(classname) ID(group)                                 
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - 'resource'                                                         
             CLASS(classname)                                                   
             ID(group)                                                          
                                                                                
  EXAMPLE  - RDELETE $TSTVS.* CLASS(FACILITY) ID(ADMIN)                         
                                                                                
  OR       - RDELETE $TSTVS.* CLASS(FACILITY) ID(ALL)                           
                                                                                
  NOTE     - ID(ALL) deletes all $TSTVS.* records, including                    
             the universal access record.                                       
             This record is the record without the GROUP and                    
             are created by ADDSD or RDEFINE.                                   
                                                                                
  The operands can be shortened to the shortest unique abbreviation.            
  So, RDELETE $TSTVS.* C(FACILITY) I(ADMIN) is also valid.                      
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The resource is created.                                               
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))'resource' - the generalized resource in the specified class. The             
  length can be up to 44 bytes. Generic resources can be created.               
))CLASS - Specify the name of the generalized resource class. The               
  class name is alphabetic value with a length up to 8 characters.              
))ID    - Specify the name of the group that grants access. The                 
  group name is alphabetic value with a length up to 8 characters.              
  If ALL is specified, all records of 'resource' are deleted,                   
  including the universal access record.                                        
                                                                                
